  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Conservation Livelihoods Approaches Around the WA-Peninsular National Park &#x2013; Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201C;Integrated Conservation Livelihoods Approaches around the Western Area Peninsular National Park (Aberdeen) &#x2013; Phase 2&#x201D; builds on the gains made in the Phase 1 piloted project. The Phase II will strengthen the gaps identified in Phase I to enhance more concrete evidence of the conservation livelihood approach and translate the reflections from the After-Action Review. Based on the documented lessons learnt, the Phase 1 project faced challenges in the implementation, especially with regards the maintenance of the planted mangroves propagules, and ineffectiveness in identifying alternative livelihood option for people engaged in environmental conservation practices for their livelihood.
The project will continue to enhance environmental conservation efforts around the Aberdeen and Big Water communities while promoting environmentally friendly livelihoods activities. The project will promote good environmental livelihood activities that promote agroforestry, and actively monitor the beneficiaries of the livelihood support to ensure their businesses becomes a success as they transition back into their gardening activities in the next planting season. The Village Saving and Loan Association (VSLA) scheme will be introduced in this second phase of the project to ensure they nurture the culture of savings from their harvests and financial gains in businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
